            "It expresses a view about the\ntransformative nature of film that film\nhistorians tend to regard as naïve.",
            "It is more motivated by a perception of the\nsignificance of the invention of film than\nby facts.",
            "It reflects a misconception that is widely\nbelieved because it captures early film\naudiences' sense that the new medium was\nalarming."
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is C (Answer Key: Topic 11, Q12). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
